"complaining. Why do people throw out water, fi-

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.860
Aww just one water? Mary Jane! Come on!

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.640
Mary Jane!

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.200
You- you're lucky I'm going to give you food.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:04.880
Dammit.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.820
Fine, have some food. Whatever.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.740
Water too, I guess. God damn it!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.760
*angry sigh* Alright. Ted!

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:14.860
Ted's my man!

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.300
Ted's my man! (2x)

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:16.820
Ted's my man! (3x)

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:17.520
He's gonna go out.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.960
"The siblings are back! Their group is growing bigger

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.480
"with each passing day, they pick up tired and hungry

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:24.440
"survivors and nurse them back to health. However,

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:26.300
"so far, they only have one tent and soon they will run out

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:28.100
"of space for everybody. Right now they're scouting the

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.100
"town for a good spot to build a bigger camp and they

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:31.760
"could really use a map." I have a map!

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:33.060
I have a map!

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.220
I have a map! (2x)

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.560
I have a map! (3x)

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.220
By the way, we're surviving a lot longer

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:39.180
than the tutorial said we'd be surviving.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.420
"They didn't have to ask twice - these people are very

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:45.060
"friendly, and the way they take care of others is impressive.

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:46.560
"We showed them the map and pointed out a few bandit

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:48.560
"camps that they should avoid. They were grateful and

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:50.560
"stayed for a little chat. They said they would be more

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.980
"than happy if we came to visit them once their camp is

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:54.800
"ready. We can't wait to see how it turns out."

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:56.660
Mary Jane is hungry. Timmy's hungry.

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.800
See... Timmy needs water.

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:02.980
Dolores has to drink. Ted wishes for a few drops of water.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.660
Okay, they can survive. We need to be very

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:09.240
stringent about that because I don't know

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:10.400
...

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:12.400
I don't know if I... I don't know if I should... Ted...

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:13.400
Send Ted out.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:17.840
You know what? I gotta send Ted out.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:19.120
'Cuz if we...

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:21.360
If we just stay here, we're not going to be doing good.

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:26.260
Take the padlock!

00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:27.920
Because I don't know what that's going to do for us.

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:29.440
If I need the padlock

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:32.780
right soon, I'm going to be very upset.

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:35.580
But... it's okay... we'll be fine.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.380
Everything's going to be fine.

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:40.300
Mary Jane needs food. Timmy needs water and food.

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:41.820
Dolores needs water.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:45.040
Food. Water. Water, food.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:47.040
That was right, right?

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.040
Timmy hungry and water. Dolores water.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:51.920
[muttering]

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:54.540
"We heard barking, we were at the door in a moment's

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:56.540
"notice. This time we were right - it was Pancake!

00:22:56.540 --> 00:22:58.920
"He had come back, but wasn't willing to enter.

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:01.200
"Instead, he seemed very anxious to lead us somewhere

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:02.920
"Should we grab any gear before we head out?"

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.020
How about the gun? Gun sounds good.

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:07.460
Gun sounds gooooood

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:08.880
Gun sounds real good.

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:11.580
Alright. Goodie goodie gumdrops.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:13.300
Maybe the map. I don't know.

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:16.000
Map? Gun? I could lose the map.

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:16.840
[inhaling through gritted teeth]

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:18.740
Eenie meanie miney moe, catch a tiger by the toe

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:19.780
Which one should I do?

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:20.820
Which one should I do? (2x)

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:22.300
Which one should I do? (3x)

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:23.480
Alright GUN!

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:27.740
[anxious silence]

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.020
[coughing sounds]

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:32.500
Yeeee. We look in bad shape.

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:34.220
"The old saying goes 'better safe than sorry.' The rifle

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.220
"seemed to be the right choice of gear for venturing into

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.220
"the unknown. We didn't expect to run into trigger happy

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:40.220
"folk who started shooting before asking questions.

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:41.960
"Gunshots were enough to send Pancake running. We

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:44.220
"got back to safety, but he didn't show up." WHAT?!?!

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:48.960
Is that good or bad? I don't understand what-

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:50.400
Aww.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.040
Mary Jane can survive longer.

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:56.760
I don't know if that's good or bad!

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.760
"Remember that time Mary Jane went out to scavenge

00:23:58.760 --> 00:24:00.760
"supplies? When she got back, she had a wound on her

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:03.780
"forearm. Nothing..." Something had bitten her?

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:06.240
Aw, I don't have the- OH MAN

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:08.240
THE AXE? Just to chop it off?

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:10.200
That seems a little extreme, don't you think?

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:13.360
Did she get bit by a radioactive spider?

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:14.840
Oh god, that doesn't look good.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:16.600
That looks very bad. Oh no.

00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:18.640
"Mary Jane will be fine. It's not the first time and it won't

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:21.680
"be the last time she's sick. She is looking pale today, though."

00:24:21.680 --> 00:24:23.200
... keeps fainting. She needs water.

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:26.460
Oh boy. Water for Mary Jane.

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:29.700
Oh man, we are in dire straits. We gotta get- *gasp*

00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:33.220
YES! OH! Yes! Map! Oh, man.

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:35.520
I could have lost the map if I went out with the map last time.

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:36.980
So this is GOOD

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:40.380
Okay! Okay! Okay! Okay! We're going to get rescued.

00:24:40.380 --> 00:24:41.620
We're gonna be fine. We're gonna get rescued.

00:24:41.620 --> 00:24:42.900
And it's gonna be a-okay.

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:44.220
Ted, I don't...

00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:47.940
"Ted has been outside for far too long and still he has not returned."

00:24:48.080 --> 00:24:48.580
WHAT!

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:50.560
"We fear he isn't coming back"!?!?!?!

00:24:50.720 --> 00:24:51.600
[distressed] Ted!

00:24:52.280 --> 00:24:53.940
Oh nohohoho!

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:57.360
Timmy! What!

00:24:59.380 --> 00:24:59.960
Huh?

00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:02.440
HUH?!?!?!

00:25:02.820 --> 00:25:05.000
"Timmy was very sick and there was nothing we could have done to make it better"

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:09.240
"He understood it and probably decided he's better off away from such irresponsible parents!"

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:12.280
"He left and never came back!?!" WHY IS THIS ALL FALLING APART NOW?!?

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:18.960
UAHHHA! But I ca- I take care of them!

00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:21.360
I took care of them!

00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:23.820
But I took care...

00:25:23.820 --> 00:25:25.480
"Where did that green puddle come from? Oh dear

00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:27.480
"a pipe is leaking green goo. That's not good.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:28.840
"We need to act. What should we do?"

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:30.640
Oh man.

00:25:31.660 --> 00:25:33.860
Why is this all falling apart now?

00:25:34.280 --> 00:25:36.420
It's day 35. Jeez.

00:25:36.880 --> 00:25:37.960
Jeez, man!

00:25:38.300 --> 00:25:39.140
Oh no.

00:25:40.740 --> 00:25:42.420
Oh no. (2x)

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:45.280
Oh no. (3x)

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:47.280
I'm not sending anyone else outside.

00:25:47.280 --> 00:25:49.280
Because I'm not leaving. No way!

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:50.900
No I'm not. It's not happening.

00:25:50.900 --> 00:25:52.360
We're going to stay in this little shelter.

00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:55.340
Dolores is going to stay down here because Dolores can last a long time

00:25:55.340 --> 00:25:57.900
by herself! Until she needs to get rescued!

00:25:58.480 --> 00:26:00.860
Why is Ted gone forever?

00:26:00.860 --> 00:26:05.560
"Ohh dammit! Something blew up inside the radio and the wretched thing caught fire!"

00:26:06.120 --> 00:26:08.380
Oho nohohohoho

00:26:10.040 --> 00:26:12.040
OH NO

00:26:13.480 --> 00:26:16.580
"When we opened the bunker door this morning to let some fresh, radioactive air

00:26:16.580 --> 00:26:19.840
"we discovered a small suitcase... no note on it..."

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:21.800
"Should we take a look inside?" Absolutely,

00:26:21.800 --> 00:26:25.400
we should look inside because WHAT ELSE CAN GO WRONG?

00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:27.660
Oh no.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:32.220
"Damn it, the gift was booby trapped. There was nothing

00:26:32.220 --> 00:26:35.000
"inside but some junk and as soon as we opened it, it exploded.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:35.900
"Is anybody hurt?"

00:26:35.900 --> 00:26:37.900
It just exploded!?!

00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:39.120
OH GOOD!

00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:40.900
Oh man.

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:44.420
Mary Jane needs water. They both need water.

00:26:44.420 --> 00:26:46.420
And now, Dolores is hurt.

00:26:46.420 --> 00:26:49.800
How is she hurt? Oh, her legs been blown.

00:26:50.080 --> 00:26:53.120
GOOD. GREEEEEAT!

00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:54.900
GREEEEEAAAAAAAAT!

00:26:55.320 --> 00:26:57.440
"We were afraid we wouldn't hear back again,

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:58.380
but our friends are back!

00:26:58.380 --> 00:27:01.040
The siblings have proudly declared that their camp is ready

00:27:01.040 --> 00:27:03.040
but they had one more thing in mind for it - a school.

00:27:03.040 --> 00:27:05.040
"They want to somehow educate the children that live there.

00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:08.220
They already appointed a few people to teach, but they're a bit short on reading material."

00:27:08.220 --> 00:27:09.700
I've got nothing, unfortunately!

00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:12.220
I never ever ever picked up the survival guide.

00:27:12.460 --> 00:27:13.940
So I'm boned on that one.

00:27:13.940 --> 00:27:15.760
"When emptying our bucket in front of the shelter,

00:27:15.760 --> 00:27:18.380
we discovered a hastily drawn map on one of the ruined walls."

00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:20.380
"Someone drew out a route and marked a spot at the end of it,

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:22.220
maybe there are supplies hidden there?" We should check.

00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:24.660
Mary Jane, go for it! You got it!

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.080
I believe in you!

00:27:26.560 --> 00:27:28.700
Go on! Get up there!

00:27:29.380 --> 00:27:31.280
That doesn't seem good that she's not back.

00:27:31.480 --> 00:27:34.060
"Mary Jane was supposed to be back in a few days, but it's been too long."

00:27:34.060 --> 00:27:37.520
"We fear something bad has happened to her?" Oh, come on!

00:27:38.260 --> 00:27:42.780
"Luckily- lucky find! We were afraid the map was a trap, leading us straight into a camp full of bandits,"

00:27:42.780 --> 00:27:44.220
"but it turned out to be true!"

00:27:44.220 --> 00:27:47.320
"At the end of the path, we found some supplies that might be helpful for us."

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:48.320
Mary Jane...

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.200
There was no point in you going there.

00:27:51.660 --> 00:27:52.540
There was no point.

00:27:52.880 --> 00:27:53.740
There was no point.

00:27:54.360 --> 00:27:58.540
"The raider camp on our street has been especially maddening lately, they're acting like real savages."

00:27:58.540 --> 00:28:00.020
"We won't stand for that, somebody should show them

00:28:00.020 --> 00:28:02.920
that the innocent survivors of the wasteland aren't just miserable victims."

00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:06.420
Okay, Delores. Go out in a blaze of glory!

00:28:06.420 --> 00:28:09.160
You shoot 'em up, you bang bang boombidie bang-

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:10.040
Oh! You're alive!

00:28:10.040 --> 00:28:11.520
Wow, that's actually kind of amazing.

00:28:12.300 --> 00:28:16.340
"We bravely stormed into the camp screaming insults and threats at the top of lungs,"

00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:20.000
meaning Delores did this by herself, just an old-school mum, just like

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:21.720
*high-pitched* 'AHHH! STOP ALL THAT!'

00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:22.940
BANG! BANG! BANG!

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:24.060
*high-pitched* 'You're dead now!'

00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:27.280
That was the best impression of a soccer mum that I could possibly do.

00:28:27.500 --> 00:28:29.820
Soccer mum to no husband and no children anymore...

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:30.780
Well, that's sad.

00:28:31.080 --> 00:28:32.800
"Sadly, there was no one there to appreciate our courage,

00:28:32.800 --> 00:28:35.060
it looks like the bandits went raiding and left the camp empty

00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:36.700
thinking no one would dare get close to it anyway!"

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:39.660
"But not us! We fearlessly collected whatever we could from their supplies

00:28:39.660 --> 00:28:41.660
and courageously ran back to our shelter."

00:28:41.660 --> 00:28:44.400
"We think it's the ultimate proof that we're not in danger - we are the danger!"

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:45.800
We ARE the danger.

00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:47.160
Okay.

00:28:47.460 --> 00:28:50.020
And apparently I can do something about Delores' injuries now!

00:28:50.280 --> 00:28:51.720
She's gonna survive!

00:28:52.400 --> 00:28:55.480
She's gonna survive alone, but she's gonna SURVIVE, dammit!

00:28:56.440 --> 00:28:59.020
Where the god damn's our rescue? Holy tits.

00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:00.140
Uh-oh, she's not doing good.

00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:01.880
But I just- But-

00:29:03.020 --> 00:29:06.280
"Her sanity's questionable"? Oh no, is that because she's got no one?

00:29:06.520 --> 00:29:08.820
Eat some food and water! Tha-that'll help you!

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:11.060
You're confident you'll survive outside?

00:29:11.060 --> 00:29:13.420
"Wasteland is full of supplies, like this man knocking on the other side of the door,

00:29:13.420 --> 00:29:15.880
knocking, claiming that he's willing to offer a lot for decent ammunition."

00:29:16.320 --> 00:29:17.140
"Shall we trade?"

00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:18.720
Okay, I've got decent ammunition.

00:29:18.940 --> 00:29:21.660
I don't think the checkerboard's good enough, but I've got decent ammunition!

00:29:22.100 --> 00:29:23.520
I don't know what good this is gonna do me,

00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:25.280
I already banged it all in the bandit camp!

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:28.380
Did I get anything in return?

00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:29.320
Mmm?

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.060
"We handed the ammunition to the stranger and he offered-

00:29:32.060 --> 00:29:33.600
OHH, THANK YOU.

00:29:33.840 --> 00:29:36.880
THANK YOU VERY MUCH BUT DELORES ISN'T DOING SO GOOD.

00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:38.960
DELORES ISN'T HOME RIGHT NOW.

00:29:39.180 --> 00:29:41.720
"Another radio broadcast from the military was a huge shock for us."

00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:45.640
"Not only did they postpone our rescue, they also ordered all survivors to get rid of their firearms."

00:29:45.640 --> 00:29:47.500
"Are they nuts? How are we supposed to defend ourselves?"

00:29:47.500 --> 00:29:49.380
"It'd better be worth it." Alright, whatever.

00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:51.060
Fine then! I guess.

00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:54.280
What more could go wrong? Delores is almost bonkers-cuckoo!

00:29:54.280 --> 00:29:55.220
*Sucks in a breath*

00:29:55.220 --> 00:29:56.200
Oh no.

00:29:57.560 --> 00:30:01.280
"We decided to follow the military orders, we did it with a heavy heart, but if it's the price of getting to safety-"

00:30:01.280 --> 00:30:04.300
Alright. Well, getting the family to safety.

00:30:04.300 --> 00:30:06.740
Um, you mean Delores, who's half-gone.

00:30:07.260 --> 00:30:08.680
"Sanity is very questionable."

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:10.000
How 'bout... nothing?

00:30:10.280 --> 00:30:11.080
You get nothing.

00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:12.520
How 'bout- how bout'-

00:30:12.520 --> 00:30:14.720
How 'bout water? How 'bout water? You get water.

00:30:15.940 --> 00:30:16.720
*sigh*

00:30:17.460 --> 00:30:18.780
45 days-o!

00:30:18.780 --> 00:30:19.800
45 days!

00:30:20.440 --> 00:30:23.240
45 days in the apocalypse, lovely lovely time.

00:30:24.060 --> 00:30:25.380
Why did Ted have to go?

00:30:27.820 --> 00:30:30.980
"Everything seems okay with Delores." I'm not a hundred percent sure about that!

00:30:31.540 --> 00:30:33.220
I'm pretty sure that's the opposite of the truth.

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:36.260
"We got a visit today from a person with a physical mutation -

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:38.880
he managed to grow several extra fully operational hands!"

00:30:38.880 --> 00:30:41.000
"He shared the story of his group with us -

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.860
people with other deformities, who despite the circumstances remain friendly

00:30:43.860 --> 00:30:45.560
and struggle to gather supplies."

00:30:45.560 --> 00:30:48.240
"Wherever they go, people just shoo them away in fear of getting sick."

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:50.460
"He promises that if we gift him some supplies,

00:30:50.460 --> 00:30:53.220
his group will help us get rid of bandits next time they bother us."

00:30:53.220 --> 00:30:54.980
Okay, I think I got soup to spare.

00:30:55.220 --> 00:30:56.380
Why not? Y'know what?

00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:57.440
Why not?

00:30:57.820 --> 00:30:58.660
Why not?

00:30:59.100 --> 00:30:59.960
WHY NOT?

00:31:01.100 --> 00:31:03.820
"Day 47". Shocked if I make it to 50.

00:31:05.780 --> 00:31:08.180
"It feels good to have some friends in this cruel, empty wasteland."

00:31:08.180 --> 00:31:11.540
"A few of our supplies is a small price to pay when it comes to the safety of your family."

00:31:11.540 --> 00:31:13.900
Once again, just Delores sitting alone in the basement!

00:31:13.900 --> 00:31:14.860
All by herself!

00:31:14.860 --> 00:31:18.160
With no one to keep her company but the radiation and the sounds of a clicking radio.

00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:20.160
And the rats! Don't forget the giant rats!

00:31:20.160 --> 00:31:22.160
And the giant fluffy bunny named Fluffernutter.

00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:24.920
"Someone paid us a visit today - it was an overly cheerful red haired woman,

00:31:24.920 --> 00:31:28.200
accompanied by a grumpy looking mercenary-type who was probably her guard."

00:31:28.200 --> 00:31:33.080
"She told us she was a trader and she'd eagerly trade us some things for some things!"

00:31:33.400 --> 00:31:35.120
Bug spray for a gas mask.

00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:36.760
Medkit for bullets.

00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:38.580
I-I only have a gas mask.

00:31:39.040 --> 00:31:40.300
Is that gonna do good enough?

00:31:41.340 --> 00:31:42.720
Alright, whatever. We're gonna try it.

00:31:43.220 --> 00:31:46.480
'Cause I've got nothing better to do and I'm pretty sure Delores is on her way out.

00:31:46.480 --> 00:31:47.860
I made it to 50 somehow!

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:49.880
Don't know how, but I did it.

00:31:49.880 --> 00:31:53.440
And then I'm gonna send Delores off into the wasteland with nothing else but bugspray.

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:55.140
Yep.

00:31:55.420 --> 00:31:56.400
Anyway, what was that?

00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.660
Uh, "her advice seems pretty useless."

00:31:58.660 --> 00:32:02.140
"We already know that radiation is dangerous and that hitting a rat with a stick will eventually kill it."

00:32:02.340 --> 00:32:04.040
Okay! Good job, trader lady!

00:32:04.560 --> 00:32:05.060
Alright.

00:32:07.020 --> 00:32:07.920
*blows out his frustration*

00:32:08.240 --> 00:32:09.540
Off you go then!

00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:14.260
You go with the industrial bug spray and you have a good time out there, Delores.

00:32:14.260 --> 00:32:16.080
You have a good time, even though you're crazy.

00:32:16.780 --> 00:32:17.680
She's not gonna make it.

00:32:17.920 --> 00:32:19.400
"The End." That's the end!

00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:21.100
Tha- Whoa, that's a new screen.

00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:23.160
Holy crap, what the hell is that?

00:32:23.400 --> 00:32:25.100
Why is the mailman out there?

00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:26.660
Well, this is a completely new screen.

00:32:27.300 --> 00:32:30.260
Oh. "We found access to our house restricted by concrete barriers

00:32:30.260 --> 00:32:33.380
and a small platoon of heavily-armed soldiers patrolling the area around it"?

00:32:33.380 --> 00:32:34.360
"We thought that's our ticket out of here,

00:32:34.360 --> 00:32:37.900
but they just took everything we had and chased us off into the wasteland."

00:32:37.900 --> 00:32:40.880
"Guess we'll be hunter-gatherers now. Like in the good old stone-age days!"

00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:41.380
WHAT!?

00:32:42.140 --> 00:32:42.880
HUH!?

00:32:43.620 --> 00:32:46.060
WHY DID THEY WALL OFF OUR HOUSE?

00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:48.800
WELL THAT DOESN'T MAKE ANY SENSE!

00:32:49.480 --> 00:32:51.720
Wha- we didn't get rescued?

00:32:52.780 --> 00:32:53.700
HUH?!?

00:32:54.100 --> 00:32:55.700
WH-WHAT?

00:32:57.840 --> 00:32:59.360
Was that the point of that?

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:02.600
Was that the point that they would never rescue us in the first place?

00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:06.720
That's not how the game would end and I had to trust like, twins doing their thing?

00:33:06.720 --> 00:33:08.300
Is that how it's supposed to be?

00:33:09.360 --> 00:33:10.200
What?

00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:13.500
Oh, my goodness!

00:33:13.500 --> 00:33:15.660
"The Government took over our shelter."

00:33:16.100 --> 00:33:18.160
Well. Wunderbar! [German for 'Wonderful']

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:19.800
That's no good!

00:33:20.180 --> 00:33:23.340
Even the mailman, who probably was telling us that we're all gonna be a-okay

00:33:23.340 --> 00:33:25.280
and we could go out and have fun.

00:33:26.180 --> 00:33:29.240
Well. I survived for 55 days on my own.

00:33:29.900 --> 00:33:31.900
Ted is dead somewhere in the wasteland.

00:33:31.900 --> 00:33:33.260
"You were driven away."

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:35.560
Oh that's new! Thank you!

00:33:36.400 --> 00:33:38.380
Driven away into where?

00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:41.900
Alright, anyway. That's all the time I have for 60 Seconds.

00:33:42.380 --> 00:33:45.420
Ahh, tell me what I did wrong in the comments below,

00:33:45.420 --> 00:33:47.020
probably I just didn't have enough stuff

00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:49.580
that I was supposed to be able to do everything that I needed to.

00:33:49.580 --> 00:33:52.240
And the expeditions somehow went very awry.

00:33:52.420 --> 00:33:54.940
So anyway, thank you all so much for watching,

00:33:54.940 --> 00:33:58.740
I hope to get back to this in a new episode and do WAY better very soon.

00:33:58.740 --> 00:34:00.740
So thanks again, and as always,

00:34:00.740 --> 00:34:02.120
I will see YOU

00:34:02.120 --> 00:34:03.440
in the next video!

00:34:03.440 --> 00:34:04.720
Buh-bye!

00:34:04.720 --> 00:34:15.200
[Outro music: Crazy La Paint by MiniMusicMan]

